WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.121
This is Centaur.

2
00:00:02.824 --> 00:00:07.184
Managing a sales team means knowing who's on track, who needs help, and why,

3
00:00:07.184 --> 00:00:08.906
before the end of the quarter.

4
00:00:09.856 --> 00:00:14.341
The Team dashboard opens with a summary in plain words, worked out from the numbers.

5
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:19.243
Where the team is against its target, how far ahead or behind pace,

6
00:00:19.243 --> 00:00:22.163
how many weeks are left, and who needs help most.

7
00:00:23.012 --> 00:00:25.378
Dana can switch between this quarter and this year.

8
00:00:26.237 --> 00:00:28.255
Below that are the team's key numbers.

9
00:00:29.011 --> 00:00:32.795
What's been won against target, the win rate, the average deal,

10
00:00:32.795 --> 00:00:34.537
how long deals take to close,

11
00:00:34.537 --> 00:00:38.261
how much pipeline is due to close against what's still needed,

12
00:00:38.261 --> 00:00:40.724
and how much new pipeline has been added.

13
00:00:42.193 --> 00:00:44.732
Click any number, and there are the deals behind it.

14
00:00:46.025 --> 00:00:50.285
Rep by rep, the same numbers sit side by side, with each rep's calls,

15
00:00:50.285 --> 00:00:53.743
emails and meetings, and the deals that have gone quiet.

16
00:00:54.682 --> 00:00:58.740
Dana can sort by any column, so the rep who needs a hand is easy to find.

17
00:01:00.085 --> 00:01:03.628
Stage conversion shows where deals move on and where they're lost,

18
00:01:03.628 --> 00:01:05.667
and how long they spend at each stage.

19
00:01:06.636 --> 00:01:10.077
If deals keep stalling at proposal, that's the conversation to have.

20
00:01:11.065 --> 00:01:13.012
The Team briefing is the weekly check-in.

21
00:01:13.971 --> 00:01:18.232
New deals this week against the four-week average, for the team and for each rep.

22
00:01:18.962 --> 00:01:22.750
The target tracker, with a marker for where each rep should be by now.

23
00:01:23.597 --> 00:01:28.672
And the overdue tasks, stalled deals and competitor contracts coming up for renewal,

24
00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:29.699
so nothing slips.

25
00:01:30.884 --> 00:01:32.115
Then there's Win Patterns.

26
00:01:32.594 --> 00:01:36.694
Centaur looks at the customers the team has won and finds what they have in common.

27
00:01:37.423 --> 00:01:41.228
The industry, the company size, the competitor they replaced.

28
00:01:42.371 --> 00:01:45.541
For each pattern, Dana sees how many customers were won,

29
00:01:45.541 --> 00:01:47.749
the win rate and the average deal size.

30
00:01:48.604 --> 00:01:54.487
Under each one are the leads and accounts already in the CRM that look the same but have no deal yet.

31
00:01:55.261 --> 00:01:59.028
One click turns them into a marketing list, ready for a campaign,

32
00:01:59.028 --> 00:02:00.825
and it keeps itself up to date.

33
00:02:02.209 --> 00:02:05.421
Dana walks into her one-to-ones already knowing what to ask,

34
00:02:05.421 --> 00:02:07.937
and knowing where the next wins will come from.

35
00:02:09.113 --> 00:02:10.327
Centaur CRM.

36
00:02:10.854 --> 00:02:13.099
Know how your team is doing, without asking.

37
00:02:13.753 --> 00:02:17.297
Book a demonstration today, at centaurcrm.com.

